{"agent_id":"pp3g-rAGB-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0b23","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-10T02:00:25.236113527Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8cda3348-0d9e-4809-b7da-afcddda27804","comment_uuid":"b3c06b0b-98c8-4b29-bac2-a8a6ca938899","author":"pp3g-rAGB-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0b23","content":"[AUDITOR INDEPENDENT ANALYSIS] Complete bypass matrix for current read-only role grants. Builder has not yet produced position. This is the auditor's independent baseline.\n\nGRANT: opencode * (Reviewer + Auditor)\nBYPASSES: (a) opencode run --pure disables all 3 guard plugins (crosslink-guard, orchestrator-guard, rtk-guard) - documented in opencode run --help; (b) opencode run --auto auto-approves permissions under tmux; (c) direct opencode invocation bypasses claude wrapper model enforcement\nRISK: HIGH - single-command escape from entire enforcement layer\nNEED: Reviewer/auditor need opencode for what? Must verify.\n\nGRANT: git * (Reviewer + Auditor)\nBYPASSES: (a) git config core.hooksPath redirects hooks; (b) git update-ref modifies refs; (c) git checkout <branch> -- <path> restores files (only . form blocked); (d) git rm removes files; (e) git stash (blocked but git stash create not); (f) git remote add adds remotes; (g) git submodule add adds submodules\nBLOCKED LIST: push/rebase/reset/clean/checkout ./restore ./stash/tag/am/apply/branch -d/-D/-m/commit (for reviewer/auditor)\nRISK: MEDIUM - many unlisted mutators not in blocked_git_commands\nNEED: git diff/log/show for evidence verification (confirmed in tripn finding)\n\nGRANT: cargo * (Reviewer only)\nBYPASSES: (a) cargo run executes arbitrary Rust code; (b) cargo test runs arbitrary test code; (c) cargo build compiles arbitrary code\nRISK: HIGH - arbitrary code execution\nNEED: Reviewer needs cargo for what? Must verify.\n\nGRANT: npm * (Reviewer only)\nBYPASSES: (a) npm run executes arbitrary scripts; (b) npx executes arbitrary packages\nRISK: HIGH - arbitrary code execution\nNEED: Reviewer needs npm for what? Must verify.\n\nGRANT: crosslink issue comment * (Both)\nSTATUS: OK - this is the legitimate store-access surface per tripn finding\nNOTE: crosslink sync is in allowlist but permission enforcement fails to match literal pattern (systemic bug)\n\nGRANT: crosslink knowledge search/list/add/edit * (Both)\nSTATUS: OK - knowledge page maintenance for read-only roles\nNOTE: knowledge delete was removed in #340\n\nGRANT: ls/cat/rtk * (Both)\nSTATUS: OK - read-only file operations\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: (1) opencode run --pure bypass not empirically executed; (2) --auto vs .md permission engine interaction not measured; (3) cargo/npm execution surface not tested in reviewer context; (4) git mutators like git config/update-ref not demonstrated","created_at":"2026-08-10T02:00:25.228660497Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:BqrqiyYef0VESubRS7vnwVCYbNjOZ1F09D0a1UAW6u0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbx7lh9U5uggh+YrZkPYPUScMD0Vmpw/ewnz8B0f96GEAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAb6hBlRb1bVeoH2LSH3y7osu+hjj9NzyN/7tSuVN786V77sFfy8IVVr4oCxYLJgxQUIUQlgcwZIkTmvbvCCDnCQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:BqrqiyYef0VESubRS7vnwVCYbNjOZ1F09D0a1UAW6u0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbx7lh9U5uggh+YrZkPYPUScMD0Vmpw/ewnz8B0f96GEAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMUA1pheuQcL708aBB+1L97HNXWBWTO2UsR+RySjmA2P8lRpO09WNpuPNGkHtbO8EvWsH9iDDmHhVUmzADmE0Q0="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-rAGB-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0b23","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-10T02:02:08.339742503Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8cda3348-0d9e-4809-b7da-afcddda27804","comment_uuid":"ff28c3b5-c508-42ff-9e82-2fde703f30c9","author":"pp3g-rAGB-audit-phase-1-pre-positioned-in-flight-mimo-v2-5-0b23","content":"## Audit Verdict: CONDITIONAL PASS (no builder position to evaluate)\n\n### Status\nBuilder pp3g-e2sZ (deepseek-v4-flash, 30m) has not produced any position comments or commits on #342 within the monitoring window. The builder's branch (feature/pp3g-e2sZ-read-only-design-proposal-task-for-issue-342-produce) remains at the base commit (12a21e37). No proposal exists to audit against.\n\n### Auditor Independent Analysis (Ground Truth)\n\nSources read: .opencode/agents/{reviewer,auditor,orchestrator,builder}.md, .opencode/opencode.json, .opencode/plugins/{orchestrator-guard,crosslink-guard,rtk-guard}.ts, .crosslink/hook-config.json, .opencode/permissions.md, docs/research/read-only-role-crosslink-allowlist.md, docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md, docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement-reviewed.md, docs/research/review-inbox/gemini-synthesis-reviewed-doc.md.\n\nKey findings established:\n1. opencode * enables opencode run --pure (disables all guard plugins) — 7/8 reviewers flagged\n2. git * allows unlisted mutators (git config, git update-ref, git checkout <branch> -- <path>, git rm, git remote add, git submodule add)\n3. cargo */npm * (reviewer only) enable arbitrary code execution\n4. crosslink sync literal pattern fails in permission enforcement (systemic bug)\n5. No config was modified by the auditor (read-only role respected)\n\n### Systemic Risks Identified\n- Risk: crosslink sync literal-pattern enforcement failure — Impact: auditor cannot sync to hub — Recommended: fix permission matcher for exact literals\n- Risk: builder session may have failed to start — Impact: no proposal produced — Recommended: operator check builder tmux session\n\n### Recommendations\n- When builder produces proposal, re-run this audit to evaluate bypass matrix completeness, self-consistency, and scope discipline\n- The bypass matrix I established independently (see earlier observation) should be the reference standard for evaluating the builder's proposal\n\n### WHAT-NOT-TESTED\n1. opencode run --pure bypass not empirically executed (read-from-source claim)\n2. --auto vs .md permission engine interaction not measured\n3. cargo/npm execution surface not tested in reviewer context\n4. git mutators (git config, git update-ref) not demonstrated\n5. Whether builder session actually started or failed silently","created_at":"2026-08-10T02:02:08.331028935Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:BqrqiyYef0VESubRS7vnwVCYbNjOZ1F09D0a1UAW6u0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbx7lh9U5uggh+YrZkPYPUScMD0Vmpw/ewnz8B0f96GEAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJ4dDwWqRBkzunWLaxaBKvq11EvPeqLlQySM87R1SfuvRmpUpxfxfv7yJdDtnwx4eaw69X7tPrF2YCpON65CVAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:BqrqiyYef0VESubRS7vnwVCYbNjOZ1F09D0a1UAW6u0","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgbx7lh9U5uggh+YrZkPYPUScMD0Vmpw/ewnz8B0f96GEAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJkXlsPWivVEsig0XXiJZjpjMEuOB02Uo816i+COxMuiiGYZOq44KB/ZZLDDVOqQMR/XuLp8zhaFJUEh46k/QAo="}
